      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, that equation helps clarify the temperature spike. \n\none more thing for the troubleshooting section of the exam. sometimes when people are talking about turbochargers, they mention a \"whine\" or a \"howling\" sound that seems almost... unnaturally loud or high-pitched, like it's \"screaming\" under load. technically, is there a way to describe that specific acoustic character? if the sound shifts from a normal whistle to a more erratic, piercing sound, is that usually a sign of a mechanical \"gremlin\" or some kind of internal interference within the turbine housing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
